I keep all my spare wands in sacks or bags.  Of course, not any
wand in any bag; one type definitely only goes in a sack (along
with a couple of holy water or blessed scrolls of remove
curse---just in case).

On the other hand, however, I rather prefer having at least one
of each of a few critical wands and rings in my main inventory.
What's the point of having a wand of death if you have to loose
a turn to get it out.  And rings of levitation, conflict, etc.
don't work if you keep them in the sack.  (Having your ring of
levitation blasted when you're floating over water can be a real
downer.)

Two weaponing is definitely nice, and worth giving up a bit of
AC to get (provided you've got sufficient AC otherwise).  But
reflection is more important.  And let's not overrate the
importance of hitting power.  It's definitly fun, but I just
ascended a healer with a crysknife and a couple of elven
daggers.  (The only artifact I ever saw was my quest artifact,
and I rather avoid wielding two handed weapons on the ascension
run.  I did keep it for an occasional invocation, however.)

